//@ compile-fail
//@ error-pattern: error[E001]
//@ error-pattern: expected f32
//@ description: PR #1737 w13 -- magnitude guard on float literal narrowing to f32
// Regression port of tests/witness_matrix/cases/w13_magnitude_must_reject.sio
// into the standard suite.
//
// CARDINAL NEGATIVE for the f32 lane: once float literals were allowed to
// adopt f32 from context (w11), the literal-holes round found `let x: f32 =
// 1e300` being ACCEPTED -- a literal wider than binary32's max (~3.4e38)
// silently coerced to a type that cannot represent it. The magnitude guard
// rejects out-of-range literals at check time. This witness holds that guard
// in place: accepting this program would mean an infinity (or a wrong value)
// minted with no diagnostic, which is the w4 defect class reborn through the
// literal path instead of the cast path.
//
// Measured 2026-08-16 on a fresh source build of main @ a5548481d1:
// rejected, error[E001] "this binding expects a different type ... expected
// f32", no ELF emitted.

fn main() -> i64 {
    let x: f32 = 1e300
    0
}
